<section class="project-hero">
  <a href="/" class="project-back-btn"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  <h1>WordPress Deployment with AWS CloudFormation</h1>
  <p>Provisioned a WordPress site on AWS by launching a CloudFormation stack directly from the console, learning stack management and resource automation.</p>
  <div class="project-hero-tags">
    <span>CloudFormation</span><span>EC2</span><span>IaC</span><span>AWS</span>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="project-details">
  <div class="center">
    <img src="/images/cloudformation.png" alt="CloudFormation WordPress Architecture" class="project-diagram">
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Project Overview</h3>
    <p>In this project, I deployed a <strong>WordPress application</strong> using the <strong>AWS CloudFormation Console</strong>. By uploading a CloudFormation template, I learned how AWS automatically orchestrates all required resources.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Architecture Explanation</h3>
    <div class="architecture-grid">
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🏗️ CloudFormation Stack</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Template</strong> — Defines EC2, Security Groups, MySQL</li>
          <li><strong>Console</strong> — Manual stack creation and management</li>
          <li><strong>Outputs tab</strong> — Exposes WordPress URL</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🖥️ Resources Created</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>EC2 Instance</strong> — Apache, PHP, MySQL, WordPress</li>
          <li><strong>Security Group</strong> — HTTP (80) and SSH (22)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Key Learnings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Launched and configured a <strong>CloudFormation stack manually</strong>.</li>
      <li>Understood how parameters (DB name, instance type, key pair) affect deployment.</li>
      <li>Used the <strong>Outputs tab</strong> to quickly find application endpoints.</li>
      <li>Explored the <strong>CloudFormation Designer</strong> for a visual stack representation.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Notes & Best Practices</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Automate deployments through <strong>CI/CD pipelines</strong> instead of manual console creation.</li>
      <li>Store sensitive parameters in <strong>AWS Secrets Manager</strong>.</li>
      <li>Use <strong>nested templates</strong> for modularity and reusability.</li>
      <li>Review <strong>Change Sets</strong> before applying updates to production stacks.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="center">
    <a href="/" class="btn-back"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  </div>
</div>

